-- title:
--   LEMMA 2, p. 227 — R(t)/t → 0 w.p. 1 as t → ∞
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $(\Omega,\mathcal F,P)$ is a probability space; $N=\{N(t),t\ge0\}$ is a process with values in a measurable space $S$; $A=\{A(t),t\ge0\}$ is a Poisson process at rate $\lambda>0$; $B\subseteq S$ is a set with $\{N(t)\in B\}\in\mathcal F$ for every $t\ge0$; $U(t)=\mathbf 1\{N(t)\in B\}$; the sample paths of $U$ are left continuous with right-hand limits w.p. 1; $U$ is jointly measurable on $\Omega\times[0,\infty)$; and lack of anticipation holds with respect to the joint history: for each $t\ge0$, $\{A(t+u)-A(t),u\ge0\}$ is independent of $\mathcal F_t$, the σ-field generated by $\{A(s),U(s);0\le s\le t\}$.
--
--   Let $R(t)=Y(t)-\lambda tV(t)$, $t\ge0$. Then
--
--   $$\frac{R(t)}{t}\to0\quad\text{w.p. 1 as }t\to\infty.$$
--
--   Lemma 2 is the new ingredient of the paper: the number of arrivals who find $N$ in $B$ and $\lambda$ times the time spent in $B$ grow at the same rate, path by path. Theorem 1 follows from it and the strong law $A(t)/t\to\lambda$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Lack of anticipation is assumed against $\mathcal F_t$ rather than against $\{U(s),0\le s\le t\}$ alone as in the printed LAA (p. 225). The page's proof of (6) uses this joint independence ("from LAA and the independent-increments property … for any set in $\mathcal F_t$"), and the printed LAA together with independent increments does not give it: with $U=1$ on $[0,1]$, $U=G$ on $(1,2]$, $U=0$ afterwards, where $G$ is the parity of $A(2)-A(1)$ masked by a fair bit computed from the arrival times in $[0,1]$, $G$ is independent of the future increments after time $1$, so the printed LAA holds, yet $E\{R(2)-R(1)\mid R(s),s\le1\}=\pm\lambda e^{-2\lambda}\ne0$ on an event of positive probability. The joint condition implies the printed one.
-- source:
--   Wolff, Poisson Arrivals See Time Averages, Oper. Res. 30 (1982), DOI 10.1287/opre.30.2.223, p. 227, LEMMA 2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WolffPASTA_Main_Setting

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology

namespace WolffPASTA.Main

/-- LEMMA 2, p. 227: `R(t)/t → 0` w.p. 1 as `t → ∞`.
Lack of anticipation is taken against the joint history `ℱₜ` (`LAAJoint`), the independence the
page's proof of (6) uses; the printed LAA (future increments independent of the past of `U` only)
does not imply (6) or LEMMA 1 (see the Formalization Note). -/
theorem lemma_2
    {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    {S : Type*} [MeasurableSpace S] (N : ℝ → Ω → S)
    (A : ℝ → Ω → ℕ) (lam : ℝ) (hlam : 0 < lam) (hA : IsPoissonProcess P A lam)
    (B : Set S) (hB : ∀ t, 0 ≤ t → MeasurableSet {ω | N t ω ∈ B})
    (hpath : PathRegular P (U N B))
    (hjoint : JointlyMeasurable (U N B))
    (hLAA : LAAJoint P A (U N B)) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂P, Tendsto (fun t => R (U N B) A lam t ω / t) atTop (𝓝 0) := by sorry

end WolffPASTA.Main
